# predatorctl-restore.service preferences.
#
# linuwu_sense reloads with driver defaults on every boot, and predatorctl
# has no daemon watching for that -- so without this file, whatever thermal
# profile / RGB effect / battery limiter you last set in the GUI is lost on
# reboot until you reopen the app and set it again.
#
# To opt in: copy this file to /etc/predatorctl/restore.conf (root-owned,
# not user-writable -- install.sh creates the directory but not the file)
# and uncomment/edit the lines you want, then:
#
#   sudo systemctl enable --now predatorctl-restore.service
#
# One "action=value" pair per line, same action names and value formats as
# the pkexec helper (see helper/predatorctl-helper ACTIONS/validate(), and
# "Value formats" in CLAUDE.md). Blank lines and lines starting with '#'
# are ignored. Invalid lines/values are skipped with a warning in the
# journal (`journalctl -u predatorctl-restore`), never fatal to the rest.

# platform_profile=balanced-performance
# battery_limiter=1
# lcd_override=0
# fan_speed=0,0
# four_zone_mode=1,4,100,1,0,255,120
